From 8761b1e5db0275b3abaa309f690acf35fc7b47cc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yihou <yihou@amd.com>
Date: Fri, 31 Jul 2026 10:31:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 05/25] sglang DSA: drop what main already carries, fold the
 layer into Dockerfile.sglang
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Rebasing this branch onto main applied cleanly, which was misleading: the branch
only ADDED files, so git saw no conflict with three changes main has since taken.
All three are now dropped in favour of main's:

  * deepseek_nextn_glm52_mtp_bf16.diff — main's patch_glm52_nextn_quark_exclude.py
    (0d8d0ff) makes the identical edit: same file, same line, same resulting value.
    Keeping both would have been actively broken, not merely redundant — main's
    loop runs first, so our context diff would then fail at --fuzz=0 against an
    already-edited anchor. apply_sglang_dsa_patches.sh now ASSERTS the edit as a
    prerequisite instead of making it, since that script is idempotent and would
    otherwise "skip" silently and leave GLM-5.2 MTP to die at draft weight-load.

  * build_mooncake_dmabuf.sh — main's build_mooncake_sglang.sh is a strict superset
    (same logic line for line, plus a HIP-transport gate check and build-tree
    cleanup). Ours had nothing main's lacks.

  * Dockerfile.sglang.dmabuf — main's Dockerfile.sglang now compiles the dma-buf
    branch in and switches at runtime via MOONCAKE_DISABLE_HIP_DMABUF, which is
    exactly how our runs drove it (=0). The only thing that image still added was
    the DSA patch layer, so that layer moves into Dockerfile.sglang, defaulting ON
    (APPLY_SGLANG_DSA_PATCHES=1) and placed after the existing sglang patch loop so
    its nextn prerequisite is satisfied. Set =0 to build a stock engine for A/B.

Net: three diffs instead of four, one Dockerfile instead of two, no duplicated
mooncake build script. The base tag stays pinned — the diffs apply at --fuzz=0
against 0b3bb0cb, so a base bump fails the build rather than mis-applying.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
